This project implements an Animal Verification Pipeline that determines whether an input text description matches the animal shown in an image.

Models Used
1. NER (Text Analysis)
Model: RoBERTa-base (fine-tuned)
Task: Extract mentions of animals from input text using token classification.
Tags used: O, B-ANIMAL, I-ANIMAL
2. Image Classifier
Model: ResNet-18 (modified last layer)
Task: Classify images into one of 10 animal classes:
dog, horse, elephant, butterfly, chicken, cat, cow, sheep, spider, squirrel

How to Run the Pipeline
1. Install required packages from requirements.txt
2. Run pipeline file from "run" folder in Google Collab (contains DEMO)
3. You’ll be prompted to: 
Enter a sentence (e.g. "I saw a big elephant")
Upload an image file

Model weights and tokenizer can be downloaded from Google Drive:
Classifier Weights: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Yz_DvxRTs4y0_6gBUsG1F4ODwXZgYH1w
NER Tokenizer: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Rs1c5DtyYB17zgcBK_MAFYsfAF1bklHs
NER Weights: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KkjluZVzaBcO6SmKtXjwuN8i-P_VyhSm
